      "root_cause_candidate": "The `is_bprm_creds_for_exec()` function incorrectly assumed the `struct file *` argument was always embedded within a `struct linux_binprm`, causing `container_of` to compute an invalid base address and trigger a stack-out-of-bounds read.",
      "evidence_points": "The CVE description explicitly states \"This is caused by using container_of on the *file pointer. This offset calculation is what triggers the stack-out-of-bounds error,\" and the patch removes the `is_bprm_creds_for_exec` function which contained `bprm = container_of(&file, struct linux_binprm, file);` in favor of passing an explicit `bprm_is_check` boolean."
    },
